        "name": "USN-4199-2",
        "description": "USN-4199-1 fixed several vulnerabilities in libvpx. This update provides the corresponding update for Ubuntu 14.04 ESM.  Original advisory details:   It was discovered that libvpx did not properly handle certain malformed  WebM media files. If an application using libvpx opened a specially crafted  WebM file, a remote attacker could cause a denial of service, or possibly  execute arbitrary code.",
